   image gate: house_2123_prairie chicagology_armour_photo: verdict "differs", 3 difference(s) open: the front's basement light beside the bow: the print's dark opening reads x 1877-1940 px, the render's light x 1907-1943 (its south jamb within a few px, its north jamb about 30 px, about 0.5 m, short of the print's). The print's is not under its own principal light (x 1933-1987), so it is not the bay's place that is off; a deeper reveal or the bow's junction in shadow may widen it at this print's grain, and no second picture settles which; the skyline south of the bow: the print's crested deck line stops over the bow's south edge (x about 1855 px, y 290-320) and the outline south of it stands about 25 px (about 0.45 m) lower, with a corniced, crested head over the second street dormer (cornice y 390-410, cresting y 345-375, x 1910-1985 px) — either a taller crown over the bow's stretch or the dormers' own hooded heads. The render's deck is one level and its dormers round-headed under no hood. K01's front crown (T-3283) refuses the print's north-flank dormer inside its depth and K01's hooded dormer takes only a flat-headed sash, where the print's light is round-headed; the front's south end at the print's right edge (x 1960-2000 px, y 410-530): the mansard's face turns down there, about where the 1911 sheet cuts the front's south-west corner back 1.9 m round the entrance (v 7.2 m); the render carries the full-width mansard and front past the frame (liberty L-k01-2123-prairie-3724, the cut corner not built)
